# The play-test session of an optimized build (pkp_pgo.py): the test version of the game plays this on a COPY of the player's save
# while it counts which code runs. Title -> Continue -> the world -> outdoors, then a tour: walk and run in every direction, turn the
# camera, open and leave the menu. Grammar: runtime/include/nxrt/tt_script.h; the state steps read the game's probes
# (runtime/games/pkp/test/pkp_tt_probe.cpp). Every wait that the tour needs is a state check: a run that never gets into the world,
# that plays a save from before the first house, or that never gets outdoors fails (exit 1, pkp_pgo.off_track) and is never a
# profile. The profile writer saves the counts every 10 s, so the run ends with a pause before @pass.
@timeout 0
@log PGO: start
@sleep 30000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
press A
@sleep 3000
# in the world: the game clock (the save's play time) only runs in play; 10 s of it within about 10 minutes of frames
@run 10 timeout=36000
@log PGO: in world
# a save from before the first house plays the opening instead of the island: its tutorial history is still short (the game's own
# m_tutorialHistory, probe `prog`: a new game reads 379 set bits, a save in its first house 496, a later one 615)
@assert prog >= 440
@sleep 10000
# outdoors: building interiors lie far from the island (x about 94000, the island about -5000 to 0): walk down, then left, right and
# up, pressing A for a door, until the player stands outdoors; never outdoors: no pass
stick left 0 -1
@mashuntil A every 90 until px < 50000 timeout=900 soft
stick left -1 0
@mashuntil A every 90 until px < 50000 timeout=600 soft
stick left 1 0
@mashuntil A every 90 until px < 50000 timeout=600 soft
stick left 0 1
@mashuntil A every 90 until px < 50000 timeout=600
stick left 0 0
@log PGO: outdoors
press B
@sleep 2000
press B
@sleep 4000
@log PGO: tour 1
stick left 0 1 for 240
stick left 1 0 for 180
stick left 0 -1 for 240
stick left -1 0 for 180
hold B
stick left 0.7 0.7 for 180
stick left -0.7 -0.7 for 180
release B
stick right 1 0 for 120
stick right -1 0 for 240
stick right 0 0.6 for 60
stick right 0 -0.6 for 60
press PLUS
@sleep 3000
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press B
@sleep 3000
press X
@sleep 3000
press B
@sleep 3000
@log PGO: tour 2
stick left 0 1 for 240
stick left 1 0 for 180
stick left 0 -1 for 240
stick left -1 0 for 180
hold B
stick left 0.7 0.7 for 180
stick left -0.7 -0.7 for 180
release B
stick right 1 0 for 120
stick right -1 0 for 240
stick right 0 0.6 for 60
stick right 0 -0.6 for 60
press PLUS
@sleep 3000
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press B
@sleep 3000
press X
@sleep 3000
press B
@sleep 3000
@log PGO: tour 3
stick left 0 1 for 240
stick left 1 0 for 180
stick left 0 -1 for 240
stick left -1 0 for 180
hold B
stick left 0.7 0.7 for 180
stick left -0.7 -0.7 for 180
release B
stick right 1 0 for 120
stick right -1 0 for 240
stick right 0 0.6 for 60
stick right 0 -0.6 for 60
press PLUS
@sleep 3000
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press B
@sleep 3000
press X
@sleep 3000
press B
@sleep 3000
@log PGO: tour 4
stick left 0 1 for 240
stick left 1 0 for 180
stick left 0 -1 for 240
stick left -1 0 for 180
hold B
stick left 0.7 0.7 for 180
stick left -0.7 -0.7 for 180
release B
stick right 1 0 for 120
stick right -1 0 for 240
stick right 0 0.6 for 60
stick right 0 -0.6 for 60
press PLUS
@sleep 3000
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press RIGHT
@sleep 1500
press B
@sleep 3000
press X
@sleep 3000
press B
@sleep 3000
# still outdoors (the tour did not walk into a building and stay there)
@assert px < 50000
@log PGO: end
@sleep 25000
@pass
